  "query_preview": "..\n\nThrough Saturday...\n\nIn general, upper ridging over the region will bring mostly dry \nand warm conditions for the next several days.\n\nA weak shortwave pushing through the Northern Rockies will cause \nthe surface pressure gradients to tighten along the western \nfoothills (IDA-LWT gradient of 12-15mb) and mid level winds to \nincrease (700mb winds to 40 kts) early this morning. This will \nbring windy conditions from Livingston to Big Timber and Nye this \nmorning into the afternoon hours. A Wind Advisory is in effect for\nthe Livingston and Nye areas into the afternoon, where gusts to \n60 mph are possible. Over the rest of the western foothills, gusts\nof 30 to 45 mph will be common, with breezy conditions extending \ninto central areas. Highs will push into the 60s to lower 70s \ntoday, much above normal for this time of year.\n\nHighs will drop behind today's wave into the 50s for most areas \non Monday, with another weak wave dropping into the area out of \nthe northwest on Tuesday. That will bring breezy winds to portions\nof the area (west gusts 20-40 mph) and showers to the mountains \nand foothills (15-30% chance). Upper ridging then looks to rebound\nand remain in place through the week bringing warmer and drier \nconditions. Highs will increase into the upper 50s to 60s most \ndays. Lows will range from the 30s to lower 40s most \nnights/mornings. STP",
